<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela delays Orinoco oil decision again. [CORRECTED 14:27 GMT]</title>
<headline>Venezuela delays Orinoco oil decision again. [CORRECTED 14:27 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's Congress again delayed a meeting expected to approve a $3.5 billion oil project in the Orinoco Tar Belt, congressional sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>They said the bicamaral Energy and Mines Committee, which is likely to approve the Hamaca project involving Venezuela's state oil subsidiary Corpoven (Corrects subsidiary from Maraven), ARCO, Texaco and Phillips, was now expected to meet at 1200 midday local time/1500 GMT on Wednesday.</p>
<p>((--Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
